<title>ITALY: Italy's Albacom gets go-ahead for capital increase.</title>
<headline>Italy's Albacom gets go-ahead for capital increase.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Italian telecoms joint venture Albacom on Wednesday approved as expected a planned capital increase to 82.4 billion lire from 42.7 billion.</p>
<p>Albacom groups Italian state-controlled bank BNL, media group Mediaset and British Telecommunications Plc.</p>
<p>The shareholders' meeting also named as board members Albacom's new managing director Giuliano Venturi and David Butcher, representing BT.</p>
<p>Albacom intends to compete for Italy's third licence to operate a mobile phone service when it comes up for tender by June.</p>
<p>The joint venture is also negotiating a partnership accord with state-controlled energy giant ENI's Snam which is expected to be concluded by the summer.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
